description:
A pretend C library hands out numbered resources that must be closed. The library is given; it counts how many are open so the tests can see leaks.

```cpp
namespace lib
{
    inline int openCount{ 0 };
    inline int nextId{ 1 };
    inline int open() { ++openCount; return nextId++; }
    inline void close(int id) { if (id > 0) --openCount; }
}
```

Write two RAII classes:

```cpp
class Resource
{
public:
    Resource();
    ~Resource();
    Resource(const Resource&) = delete;
    Resource& operator=(const Resource&) = delete;
    int id() const;
};

template <typename F>
class ScopeExit
{
public:
    explicit ScopeExit(F action);
    ~ScopeExit();
    void dismiss();
};
```

- **Resource** opens one resource in its constructor and closes it in its destructor. `id()` returns its number.
- **ScopeExit** runs its action when it is destroyed, unless `dismiss()` was called. Copying it is not allowed.

The tests leave scopes by falling off the end, by `return` and by exceptions, and check that every resource was closed exactly once.

